ing the failure is attributable to one of the conflated UDR or network elements rather than mongo itself.\",\n          \"conflates_with\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"Using get_network_status and check_process_listeners for direct state observation. Paired measure_rtt probes confirm network unreachability specific to mongo from a dependent NF (UDR).\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
    "investigation": "[\n  {\n    \"hypothesis_id\": \"h1\",\n    \"hypothesis_statement\": \"mongo is the source of the failure, as its container has unexpectedly exited, causing database connection failures for dependent core components (UDR, PCF, NSSF, BSF). (Per L10)\",\n    \"verdict\": \"NOT_DISPROVEN\",\n    \"reasoning\": \"[Multi-shot consensus \\u2014 both shots returned NOT_DISPROVEN.]\\n\\nShot 1: The get_network_status probe directly confirms that the mongo container is in the 'exited' and 'down_or_absent' state. Network reachability tests from udr to mongo fail due to name resolution (which is expected for a down container), while udr to nrf succeeds, confirming the failure is isolated to mongo and not a general network stack issue on udr. The hypothesis holds.\\n\\nShot 2: The network status check confirms that the mongo container is in an exited state. Network routing tests show that dependent components like UDR cannot resolve or reach mongo, while successfully maintaining reachability to other components like NRF, confirming the localized failure of the mongo container.\",\n    \"probes_executed\": [\n      {\n        \"probe_description\": \"Check network status to see if mongo container is down or exited.\",\n        \"tool_call\": \"get_network_status()\",\n        \"observation\": \"[EVIDENCE: get_network_status() -> \\\"\\\\\\\"down_or_absent\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"mongo\\\\\\\"], \\\\\\\"containers\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"mongo\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"exited\\\\\\\"}\\\"]\",\n        \"compared_to_expected\": \"CONSISTENT\",\n        \"outcome\": \"consistent\",\n        \"commentary\": \"Directly confirms the mongo container is down/exited.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"probe_description\": \"Check if mongo is listening on port 27017.\",\n        \"tool_call\": \"check_process_listeners(\\\"mongo\\\")\",\n        \"observation\": \"[EVIDENCE: check_process_listeners(\\\"mongo\\\") -> \\\"PROBE_TOOL_UNAVAILABLE: check_process_listeners cannot run on container `mongo`\\\"]\",\n        \"compared_to_expected\": \"AMBIGUOUS\",\n        \"outcome\": \"tool_unavailable\",\n        \"commentary\": \"The container was already confirmed down, but the tool itself is missing the required binary ss/netstat. No evidence gathered from this specific probe.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"probe_description\": \"Check network reachability from udr to mongo.\",\n        \"tool_call\": \"measure_rtt(\\\"udr\\\", \\\"mongo\\\")\",\n        \"observation\": \"[EVIDENCE: measure_rtt(\\\"udr\\\", \\\"mongo\\\") -> \\\"Ping failed from 'udr' to 'mongo': ping: mongo: Temporary failure in name resolution\\\"]\",\n        \"compared_to_expected\": \"CONSISTENT\",\n        \"outcome\": \"consistent\",\n        \"commentary\": \"Confirms mongo is completely unreachable from a dependent NF (udr), as expected when the container is down.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"probe_description\": \"Check network reachability from udr to nrf to isolate the failure to mongo.\",\n        \"tool_call\": \"measure_rtt(\\\"udr\\\", \\\"nrf\\\")\",\n        \"observation\": \"[EVIDENCE: measure_rtt(\\\"udr\\\", \\\"nrf\\\") -> \\\"66 packets transmitted, 66 received, 0% packet loss\\\"]\",\n        \"compared_to_expected\": \"CONSISTENT\",\n        \"outcome\": \"consistent\",\n        \"commentary\": \"Confirms the failure to reach mongo from udr is not due to a network stack issue on udr, narrowing the fault down to mongo itself.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"alternative_suspects\": []\n  }\n]",
